IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g1-first-schedule`
IMPORT `g1-interpretation`
IMPORT `g1-licensing-duty`
IMPORT `g1-adverse-action`
IMPORT `g1-tests-licensing`
IMPORT `g1-tests-adverse`

-- g1-tests-red.l4: assertions that are MEANT to fail.  Group G1.  NINETEEN assertions, all expected failed.
-- Each asserts the answer of a reading that the fork register in FRAGMENT-G1.md considered and rejected, against the
-- function that takes the OTHER reading.  Each must therefore fail while the encoding takes the reading it takes; the file
-- doubles as proof that this harness can fail.  The expected-failed count is 19 (check.sh lists it).  The fixtures come from
-- g1-tests-licensing.l4 and g1-tests-adverse.l4.

§ `Rejected readings of G1`

§§ `Fork F1: "up to 18 kW" and "up to 70 kW" read as excluding the limit`

#ASSERT NOT `s 2 — the licence kind covers the cooling system` `grade 1 licence` `a system of 18 kW`
#ASSERT NOT `s 2 — the licence kind covers the cooling system` `grade 2 licence` `a system of 70 kW`

§§ `Fork F4 (trap T9): B.1(3) and B.3(2) both reach components; the rejected reading puts a compressor replacement under B.3(2), grade 3 only`

-- `work s16` is a grade 1 licensee doing B.1(3) on a 10 kW system.  Under the rejected reading the work is B.3(2) and is forbidden.
#ASSERT `section 3(a) forbids the work` `work s16`

§§ `Fork F8: a licence that is not in force counts as a licence held (item (2)), not "no licence at all" (item (1))`

-- `work s08`: no licence in force, a licence that is not in force.  The rejected reading says item (2), "not of the appropriate kind".
#ASSERT `the outcome of section 3(a) for the work` `work s08` EQUALS `the work is forbidden: the person holds no licence of the kind appropriate to the system and the work`

§§ `Fork F9 (trap T12): work outside the conditions of a licence is work without the appropriate kind (item (2))`

#ASSERT `the listed violation committed under section 3(a)` `work s29` EQUALS JUST `work without a licence of the kind appropriate to the system`

§§ `Fork F10: the conditions of an exemption order are conditions of the exemption`

-- `work s28`: no licence, a class exempted by order.  The rejected reading says that without the order's conditions met the person is not exempt.
#ASSERT `the outcome of section 3(a) for the work` `work s28` EQUALS `the work is forbidden: the person holds no licence at all`

§§ `Fork F11: a consultation counts once held, whether or not the Council's advice was validly given (s.3(b))`

#ASSERT `the Minister may exempt classes of cooling systems by order` `an order after a consultation whose advice was not valid`

§§ `Fork F13: a licence of a higher grade is a licence "of that kind" (s.4)`

-- `self-description f03`: advertises as grade 2, holds grade 3.
#ASSERT NOT `section 4 forbids the self-description` `self-description f03`

§§ `Fork F18: the cap of s.10(a) counts the day the period begins as its first day`

#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar may take the measure under section 10(a)` `suspension on ground 5 for exactly three years`

§§ `Fork F19: IL s.10(c) applied to the three-year cap (a period of validity)`

-- `a suspension ending on the day after the nominal cap`, with 1 March 2029 a day of rest: the rejected reading moves the cap to 2 March 2029.
#ASSERT `the Registrar may take the measure under section 10(a)` `a suspension ending on the day after the nominal cap`

§§ `Fork F17: the cap of s.10(a) reaches a suspension only, not a restriction`

#ASSERT `the Registrar may take the measure under section 10(a)` `restriction on ground 2 for four years`

§§ `Fork F20: s.8 carried into ground (2): the loss of the s.6(a)(4) condition alone cannot ground a refusal to renew`

#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar may take the measure under section 10(a)` `refusal to renew where only the training condition ceased`

§§ `Fork F21: "until final judgment" stops short of the day of the judgment (s.10(b))`

#ASSERT NOT `a suspension under section 10(b) is in force on the day` (YMD 2026 5 1) (JUST (YMD 2027 6 10)) (YMD 2027 6 10)

§§ `Fork F23: the second limb of s.10(c) needs a fresh consultation of the Council`

#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar may take the measure after the cure period` `a measure after the period without consulting the Council again` `no days of rest at all`

§§ `Fork F24: the cure period counted without IL s.10(c) (kind D)`

-- The period ends on 31 January 2026 nominally, a day of rest in this calendar; the rejected reading lets the measure be taken on 1 February.
#ASSERT `the Registrar may take the measure after the cure period` `a measure on the day after the last day` `a calendar with 31 January 2026 a day of rest`

§§ `Fork F25: the Registrar's power to add conditions to a new licence needs the Council consulted (s.10(d))`

#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar may add conditions to the grant of a new licence` `a revocation without consulting the Council`

§§ `Fork F26: the bar after a revocation counted without IL s.10(c) (kind W)`

-- 2 years from 15 March 2026 end on 15 March 2028, a day of rest in this calendar; the rejected reading opens the window on 16 March.
#ASSERT `a new application may be made on the day after the bar` `a period of 2 years from 15 March 2026` `a calendar with 15 March 2028 a day of rest` (YMD 2028 3 16)

§§ `Fork F6: "monitoring, warning and control" are three functions every integral accessory must serve`

`a sensor that only monitors` MEANS `Facts about a part accompanying a system under the First Schedule` WITH
    `permanently connected to the system` IS TRUE
    `used to monitor the function of the installation` IS TRUE
    `used to warn of the function of the installation` IS FALSE
    `used to control the function of the installation` IS FALSE

#ASSERT NOT `the part is an integral control and monitoring accessory` `a sensor that only monitors`

§§ `Fork F7: the parenthesis of "integral electrical system" is only an illustration`

`a dedicated system outside the dedicated panel` MEANS `Facts about an electrical system of a cooling system under the First Schedule` WITH
    `a dedicated system forming part of the cooling system` IS TRUE
    `part of the dedicated panel of the cooling system` IS FALSE
    `supplied by the manufacturer` IS FALSE
    `supplied to the requirements of the manufacturer` IS FALSE
    `intended for the cooling system` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `the electrical system is the integral electrical system of the cooling system` `a dedicated system outside the dedicated panel`
